  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Global and Regional Futures Literacy: a PMU-UNESCO Collaborat</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Prince Mohammad Bin Fahd University and UNESCO are joining forces to cultivate world class research, teaching and intergenerational community-engagement by improving practical, contextualized capacities to understand the future. Such improvements, as UNESCO&apos;s pioneering work in the field have shown, depend on gaining a better understanding of both why and how people and organisations anticipate. To develop and strengthen such capacities regionally and globally, PMU and UNESCO will apply and test cutting-edge action-learning and action-research techniques to train PMU researchers and to be showcased to the rest of the Global Futures Literacy Network.</narrative>
  </description>
